  "live_records": {
    "q-87211": {
      "dom_id": "step-q87211",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Compute $P(4\\le X<5)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{36}x,\\, & 3\\le x\\le 9, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(4\\le X<5) & ={\\int }_{4}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{5}\\frac{1}{36}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{72}{x}^{2}]}_{4}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
