    "q-86913": {
      "dom_id": "step-q86913",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Compute $P(2<X<8)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{50}x,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 10, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X<8) & ={\\int }_{2}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{8}\\frac{1}{50}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{100}{x}^{2}]}_{2}^{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
