    "q-158459": {
      "dom_id": "step-q158459",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Compute $P(X<2)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{225}({x}^{3}-x),\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x<1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2) & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{4}{225}({x}^{3}-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{225}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{3}-x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{225}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{225}([\\frac{1}{4}(2)^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}(2)^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{4}(1)^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{2}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{225}(4-2-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{225}\\cdot \\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-158459-a",
