    "q-158363": {
      "dom_id": "step-q158363",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Compute $P(X\\le 2)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{72}({x}^{3}+x),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x<0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{72}({x}^{3}+x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{72}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}+x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{72}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{72}([\\frac{1}{4}(2)^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}(2)^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{4}(0)^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{72}(4+2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{72} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
